[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Heracles Internal and External GUI Software Failure Modes and Effects Analysis
UID: DHF-HRC-0028
METADATA:
  COMPONENT: heracles-gui-sfmea

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Purpose

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The purpose of this Software Failure Modes and Effects Analysis (SFMEA) is to evaluate the potential failure modes in the Internal and External GUI Software, understand their effects on the system, patient, and other users, prioritize risks, and recommend corrective actions to mitigate those risks. The purpose is to ensure the safety and effectiveness of the device throughout its lifecycle.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Scope

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The scope of this SFMEA covers the Internal and External GUI Software, derived from its design. This document is to be continuously maintained and updated throughout the lifecycle of the medical device, as potential software failure modes are addressed and mitigated to achieve an acceptable or As Low As Possible (ALAP) level of risk.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Abbreviations and Definitions

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
ALAP                   As Low As Possible
SDD                    Software Design Document
SFMEA                  Software Failure Modes and Effects Analysis
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Overview

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The Internal GUI console provides a means for the user to maintain demographic patient data, including treatment plans, and perform imaging. It communicates with the record and verify component, flange camera stream, imaging component and robotic arm controller.

The internal GUI software runs on the All-In-One console located on the base of the system.

The external GUI console provides a means for the user to activate and monitor the treatment. It communicates with the main control board, treatment head camera and imaging head camera.

The external GUI software runs on the external tablet console located outside the room.
<<<

