[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: SFMEA Matrix

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The following table presents the SFMEA analysis for identified failure modes in the Internal and External GUI Software:

Key Failure Modes Identified:

1. H10SG-683 - Calculate Emission Duration
   Failure Mode: Miscalculation of Emission Duration
   Sequence of Events: Calculation logic has a bug
   Initial Severity: Critical (4)
   Initial Probability: Probable (3)
   Risk Controls: Firmware will reject treatment plans exceeding 300 sec; Unit test + code review
   Residual Risk: Acceptable

2. H10TG-276 - Validate Active Collimator
   Failure Mode: Failure to validate active collimator
   Sequence of Events: Incorrect collimator identification causing system to treat patient with wrong collimator
   Initial Severity: Critical (4)
   Initial Probability: Probable (3)
   Risk Controls: Unit test + code review
   Residual Risk: Acceptable

3. H10TG-263 - Stop Emission
   Failure Mode: Emission Failed to stop
   Sequence of Events: User pressed the stop button and emission fails to stop
   Initial Severity: Critical (4)
   Initial Probability: Probable (3)
   Risk Controls: E-Stop physical switch; Unit test + code review
   Residual Risk: Acceptable

4. H10TG-257 - Record Treatment Delivered Dose
   Failure Mode: Failure to Record Treatment Delivered Dose
   Sequence of Events: Delivered no data recorded after treatment
   Initial Severity: Critical (4)
   Initial Probability: Probable (3)
   Risk Controls: Data saved to file for restoration; Alert prompt displayed to user; Unit test + code review
   Residual Risk: Acceptable

5. H10TG-257 - Record Treatment Delivered Dose (Faulty Record)
   Failure Mode: Faulty Record Data delivered
   Sequence of Events: Incorrectly recorded dose data in the database
   Initial Severity: Critical (4)
   Initial Probability: Probable (3)
   Risk Controls: Unit test + code review
   Residual Risk: Acceptable

6. H10TG-255 - Beam On Process
   Failure Mode: Failure to start emission
   Sequence of Events: User pressed the Beam-On button and emission fails to start
   Initial Severity: Major (3)
   Initial Probability: Probable (3)
   Risk Controls: Unit test + code review
   Residual Risk: Acceptable

7. H10TG-274 - Retrieve treated patient details
   Failure Mode: Wrong patient sent to application
   Sequence of Events: Operator loads patient data to external console; external console displays wrong patient data
   Initial Severity: Critical (4)
   Initial Probability: Probable (3)
   Risk Controls: Unit test + code review
   Residual Risk: Acceptable

All identified failure modes have been assessed and assigned appropriate risk control measures.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: SFMEA Risk Prioritization

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The SFMEA matrix above prioritizes identified failure modes based on their initial risk index (RI), which is calculated as the product of the probability of occurrence and the severity of potential harm. Items with higher risk indices receive priority for risk control measures.

All identified failure modes have been assessed and assigned appropriate risk control measures. Initial risk indices ranging from 9 to 12 have been addressed through design features, testing protocols, and code review processes to reduce residual risk to acceptable levels.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: SFMEA Risk Acceptability

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Risk acceptability is determined based on the residual risk index following implementation of control measures. The following acceptability zones are applied:

- Zone 1: Acceptable Risk (RI ≤ 4)
- Zone 2: ALAP (As Low As Possible) - Risk is acceptable but continuous improvement is expected (RI 5-8)
- Zone 3: Unacceptable Risk (RI ≥ 9) - Requires additional controls

All residual risk indices have been reduced to Zone 1 (Acceptable) through implementation of the recommended risk controls. Ongoing validation through unit testing, code review, and integration testing ensures that risk mitigation effectiveness is maintained throughout the product lifecycle.
<<<

